WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.830
<i>Hello, I'm Mr. Raccoon.</i>

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.460
OWNER

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.460
<i>Right now,
I'm with my owner</i>

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.710
GIRLFRIEND

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.710
<i>and his girlfriend</i>

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.380
<i>who are on their way back
from buying sweets as a study break.</i>

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.680
Your dog's cute, Nagata.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.720
Higashi, hang out with us, too.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.970
It's really cute.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.520
Higashida...

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.060
<i>I see. Now there's another
cute pet that he likes.</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.480
<i>I feel unwanted.</i>

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.240
<i>I'll just be her buddy for today.</i>

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.320
<i>Yahoo!</i>

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.740
Mr. Raccoon...

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.240
Higashi...

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.750
What's that for?

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:45.210
I'm sure you'll lose your appetite
since your own pet hates you now,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.170
so let me have those sweets.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.800
I don't care if he hates me,
and besides, these aren't my sweets.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.050
This pet forced me to buy them for her.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.050
PET?

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.640
I'm no pet!

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:34.400
IF SOMEONE HITS YOU ON THE RIGHT CHEEK,
COUNTER WITH YOUR LEFT FIST

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.650
Hey, Muranushi...

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.900
When you're dating, is it enough to have
the other person treat you to meals?

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.030
- No.
- It's not, is it?

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.530
What does it mean, Kisaki?

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.030
What, indeed.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.990
I told you before,
but you're not hurting financially,

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.750
so you shouldn't have him
treat you all the time.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.290
Then why are you going out
with Adachi?

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.630
I told you before.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.880
You should think
about the other person's feelings.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:59.340
I thought about it,
but I didn't understand!

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.600
So what does that mean?
What do I lack?

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.640
Tell me, as someone
who's in a relationship!

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:08.520
The takeaway... It's that, um...

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.190
Towards him, you need...

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.730
consideration!

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:16.610
<i>You shouldn't be the one to say that.</i>

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.320
<i>But both of these girls are troublesome.</i>

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.660
Don't think.
Hurry up with your stinging barb.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.660
Consideration...

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:28.200
Miyakoshi, I want to ask you something.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:33.590
Your boyfriend is over there
chatting chummily with another girl.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.630
What do you think when you see that?

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.010
- How's your cold?
- I'm much better now.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.220
H-Higashida, that jerk!

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:44.390
Why won't he seat that customer?

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:48.520
She's at a passionate time in her life,
but seeing that doesn't fry her...

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.730
FRY!?

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:49.730
Fry what?

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:53.360
By "being fried," I meant...
you get angry, like, "He's toast!"

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.190
Toast?

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.730
So when you're dating, you toast
rice cakes? Have you ever done that?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.440
No, can't say I have.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:01.990
Consideration...

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:05.080
Forget it. This conversation
is going nowhere.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.950
End of discussion.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.200
<i>She ended the discussion.</i>

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:17.130
MULL MULL

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.500
<i>Who else would be knowledgeable
about love and romance?</i>

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.130
<i>Another woman who works here?</i>

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.590
<i>Kamakura?</i>

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.090
Nope!

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:22.880
At least, I don't think so.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.800
What are you doing, Miyakoshi?

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:26.810
Let's go home.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:27.760
Okay.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:32.520
Higashida! You don't keep
the customers standing around!

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.020
Oh, sorry. We just started chatting.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:37.980
<i>That's it!</i>

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.400
<i>Maybe that customer knows
a lot about love and romance!</i>

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:43.950
<i>Except that customer...</i>

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.870
<i>Besides, she's gotten mad at me before.</i>

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.120
I have a good idea!

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:52.580
- I'll—
- Don't!

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.210
Don't say "don't" before I even
say what I'm gonna do!

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:58.800
It's the kindness in me that wants
to keep you from wasting words.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:00.090
Excuse me?

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.510
So what are you going to
make me pay for today?

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:07.350
It's before payday,
so please make it something cheap.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:10.060
Nothing today. I have something
to do, so I'm going right home.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.310
That's nice to hear.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:15.190
And speaking of pay,
you make me give up a lot of mine,

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.060
but how do you use
your earnings, Miyakoshi?

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.520
I think it's in the bank.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:25.070
Don't tell me you forgot your PIN number,
so you can't take out any money.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.370
Quit predicting what I'm gonna say!

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:31.620
It doesn't matter. Mom gives me
an allowance anyway, so that's enough.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.960
<i>Is it? You sponge off of me all the time.</i>

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.580
Whatever. Let's go.

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:39.630
<i>So she's not working
part-time to make money?</i>

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.550
<i>Well, that's what I imagined.</i>

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.630
<i>But then why does she work?</i>

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:49.930
<i>I remember asking her
about her family before.</i>

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.140
<i>Miyakoshi is full of mysteries.</i>

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.140
Well, see you tomorrow!

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:55.890
Oh, right.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.730
After that, I think
I'll stay over at your place!

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.110
Oh, right.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.690
Wait, what are you talking about?

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:07.660
<i>She isn't answering
her phone or my texts.</i>

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.740
<i>What's going on tomorrow?</i>

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.370
- Bro!
- Sakiko...

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.830
Mom and Dad won an overnight trip
to a hot spring in a drawing,

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.380
so they're going tomorrow.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.670
And I'm going to a study session
sleepover at a friend's house,

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.420
so you'll be all alone here
tomorrow night.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:28.260
<i>After that, I think
I'll stay over at your place!</i>

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.810
Don't leave me here alone!

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.310
What are you talking about?
You're a high school student!

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:40.060
I mean, when I left the house,
Mom's face was as white as a sheet.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.270
I hope it'll be okay.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:43.900
I didn't catch it yesterday, but...

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:47.650
Miyakoshi, why are you here today?

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:49.910
Weren't you listening?

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:53.660
What the hell? You gotta listen
when someone's talking to you.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.500
Are you gonna make me say it again?

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.000
I'm nervous about this myself.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.920
You're as pale as Mom was!

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:07.470
Jeez. What are you so afraid of?

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:10.090
Nothing bad's gonna happen to you.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:10.930
TA-DA

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.680
<i>Sure enough!</i>

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.600
I'm gonna eat this!

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:17.180
Wait! Um, huh?

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:21.150
That old man brought it up, so he's gotta
know a lot about love and romance!

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:25.780
I used leftover ingredients from last time
to make one piece of chocolate!

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.190
It's a little embarrassing
for me to admit it,

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:32.160
but I'm sure this is so awful that if I eat it,
I'll be able to go see the old man!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.740
And if I do it at your house,

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:37.750
Mom or the customers won't worry
or get angry at me!

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.120
I'm clever!

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:42.920
And since there's only one piece,
you won't get hurt, Higashida.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.920
<i>It's an idiotic yet detailed plan!</i>

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:50.130
<i>And since she's an idiot, she isn't thinking
about the consequences to her own life!</i>

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:52.180
- Miya—
- Well, I'll see you in a little bit.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.100
Don't die like you're just going
to the convenience store!

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:15.030
<i>How's the modern world full of love, peace
and anxiety been treating you, Earthlings?</i>

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.990
<i>Long time no see. I'm St. Valentine.</i>

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:20.040
<i>I'm tiny because it's off-season.</i>

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:21.790
<i>I know what's happening.</i>

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:25.380
<i>There aren't enough hearts that are
accepting and forgiving of each other.</i>

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.420
<i>For example, even if you were
treated shabbily in the past,</i>

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:32.130
<i>if you get revenge, there'll be
no end to it. Forgiveness is needed.</i>

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:32.130
<i>Yo!</i>

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.140
<i>What are you trying to escape for?</i>

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:39.310
<i>It's not like I'm trying to smack you
so hard your hat breaks.</i>

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.270
<i>That's exactly what you did last time!</i>

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.440
<i>Well, whatever. I'll get to the point.
I have a favor to ask.</i>

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:50.940
<i>Teach me about love, romance
and consideration in a simple way!</i>

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:55.240
<i>You're a fake Hana, aren't you?</i>

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.030
<i>Begone!</i>

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:06.580
<i>Hana, you can't learn about love
by asking someone about it.</i>

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.050
<i>You feel affection for your partner,
sometimes hate them,</i>

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:12.590
<i>and there are various
other emotions mixed in there, too.</i>

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.050
<i>For now, maybe you should go
with what Sayurin said,</i>

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:19.600
<i>to think about what would
please the other person.</i>

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.640
<i>Okay, so what about consideration?</i>

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:25.480
<i>Consideration is easy.</i>

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:29.860
<i>That's what you lack the most, Hana!</i>

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:32.530
<i>Sorry!</i>

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.280
<i>Still, it's sad that I came all this way</i>

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:37.530
<i>and didn't get any love
or romance-related results.</i>

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:38.990
<i>Look, Hana...</i>

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:43.660
<i>how is it that you can treat the customers
right, but act horribly otherwise?</i>

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.710
<i>Well, customers are customers.</i>

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.710
<i>But now that you mention it,
good question...</i>

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.920
<i>I sympathize with Higashida.</i>

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:55.800
<i>I do feel guilty about Higashida...</i>

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:59.100
<i>but I don't really know what boyfriends
and girlfriends are supposed to do.</i>

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:04.890
<i>I'm worried that you'll ask someone else
and it'll cause strange discord.</i>

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.100
<i>You want to know
what sweethearts do?</i>

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:17.070
<i>Higa...</i>

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.450
<i>- Higashida, you surprised me!
- Hi!</i>

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:22.830
<i>I'm surprised that you were
more surprised than I expected.</i>

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:26.040
<i>Well, he was telling me
some scary stuff.</i>

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:30.290
<i>To be honest, looking at you
is the scariest thing right now.</i>

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.050
<i>How did you get here?</i>

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.640
<i>Why are you still surprised
that I'm here?</i>

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:40.430
<i>After all,</i>

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:43.600
<i>I made only one small piece
so you wouldn't be dragged into it.</i>

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.390
<i>Well...</i>

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:48.310
<i>And there weren't any ingredients left.</i>

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:50.270
<i>If anything, it'd be
the chocolate in my mouth—</i>

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:53.900
<i>The one time she catches on,
at a time like this...</i>

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:54.860
<i>Even though she's dumb.</i>

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.610
<i>D-D-D-Don't tell me you...</i>

00:10:58.030 --> 00:10:58.780
<i>took—</i>

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:00.700
<i>Wait, um, please listen to me!</i>

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:04.200
<i>It was kind of inevitable!
I was reluctant to do it!</i>

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:07.460
<i>I-I'm sorry. Totally.</i>

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.420
<i>It's totally my fault!</i>

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:13.960
<i>Dammit! I'm sorry you wanted to die
so badly that you ate the chocolate!</i>

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:14.550
<i>Wait, Miyakoshi!</i>

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:17.630
<i>We both ate the chocolate,
so we're dying right now!</i>

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.140
<i>She's gone.</i>

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:22.680
<i>She wasn't worth tracking down.</i>

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:24.850
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.850
<i>I'll fix your hat.</i>

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.600
<i>Sorry for the constant hassle.</i>

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.110
<i>But I wonder if Miyakoshi is okay?</i>

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:35.360
<i>I'll return Hana to Earth,
so she'll be fine.</i>

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:38.110
<i>That aside, did you really do it?</i>

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.070
<i>Yes.</i>

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:42.240
<i>To be honest, it was disagreeable
in more ways than one,</i>

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.990
<i>and it felt like I was crossing a line...</i>

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:44.700
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:47.370
<i>...but I was worried
about something happening to her...</i>

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:48.120
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:50.870
<i>...and if Miyakoshi died like that,</i>

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:53.630
<i>I would obviously be the culprit, so...</i>

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.130
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:11:56.420 --> 00:12:00.930
<i>I ate Miyakoshi's old chocolate
which I couldn't finish back then and hid.</i>

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:02.340
<i>Higashida...</i>

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.970
<i>She did do her best to make it, after all.</i>

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.600
<i>And I have a responsibility
to not let anyone else be hurt by it,</i>

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.350
<i>so I meant to eat all of it back then...</i>

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:10.640
but after I brought it back home,

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:13.230
I had second thoughts about
the possibility of dying at the house,

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:17.650
but I couldn't toss it, and yet I was nervous
about keeping it past the expiration date!

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:18.490
Huh?

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:20.110
I'm back?

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:22.490
<i>Morning already?</i>

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:27.240
<i>If Miyakoshi isn't here, that means
she woke up and went back home, right?</i>

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:30.160
<i>Well, good. We came back alive,</i>

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.540
<i>and for now, it's over without any—</i>

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:37.050
Miyakoshi was just crying
as she left. What happened?

00:12:37.300 --> 00:12:39.050
What? What was it? What did you do?

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.050
<i>I didn't do anything.</i>

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:48.390
What's wrong, Miyakoshi?

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:51.560
Look, I'm wiping a cup.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:53.190
That's abnormal.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:56.560
You're always the one
who gets all the work done, Miyakoshi.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.110
Do you feel under the weather?

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:00.780
Listen...

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.030
Muranushi?

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:07.700
<i>The rest is up to you.</i>

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:10.910
<i>I have to deal with her alone?</i>

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.120
What is it? What's this about? What?

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:15.960
I have a question.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.790
A question? About homework?

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:21.590
I think Kisaki would know
more about that kind of stuff than me.

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:24.130
K-K-K-K-Ki-Ki...

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:25.050
Ki?

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:27.800
Have you ever kissed someone?

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:35.850
No, never.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:37.150
Why not?

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:39.690
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Why?

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:44.610
I-I-I want to do that kind of thing
with s-s-s-someone I love,

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.950
s-so it's like I'm saving it up.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:50.740
Even Kamakura treasures it!

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.160
What are you going on about?

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:57.380
It seems that even the cold Kamakura
has put a high premium on it.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.000
It's just like that old man said.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.670
Kissing is a big deal.

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:06.630
And to make him do that
without even realizing it...

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:10.180
Higashida lost something
that he can never get back.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:12.890
I'm like the character in this girls' manga.

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:15.480
<i>Too bad!</i>

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.900
<i>Technically, you had
your first kiss with me!</i>

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:18.980
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:21.610
<i>Even though I only gave you CPR
because you almost drowned!</i>

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:24.030
<i>I'm like the boy!</i>

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:25.150
Miyakoshi...

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:25.570
TWITCH

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:27.450
H-Higashida!

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:29.370
Do you feel ill?

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:30.530
No.

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:32.950
You're bothered by what happened
the other day, aren't you?

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:35.580
I wasn't thinking
of your feelings, Miyakoshi.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:38.120
In fact, I acted thoughtlessly.

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:40.960
I'm sorry. I regret what I did.

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:40.960
Talking about not eating
all of the chocolate previously.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:42.670
<i>He apologized to me!</i>

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.880
<i>I'm the one who made him do it
and he apologizes?</i>

00:14:46.170 --> 00:14:47.800
<i>What is he, a monk?</i>

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:52.220
For you to feel poorly when your
energy is your only good point...

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.230
Referring to the chocolate he kept.

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:55.230
I know how important that was to you.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.900
I'm the one who, you know...
I'm sorry!

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:02.860
<i>That's unusually humble.
For Miyakoshi...</i>

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:05.070
<i>Dammit! My head is spinning even more</i>

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:08.360
<i>thanks to what that old man told me
about love, romance and whatnot!</i>

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:12.870
<i>No, it's all my fault for going out with him
without knowing about any of that!</i>

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:17.160
Anyway, what's done is done.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:18.250
Right.

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:21.000
RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:21.000
But I will pay you back!

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.250
<i>There's the Miyakoshi I know.</i>

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:24.750
<i>Miyakoshi...</i>

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:27.880
<i>She's more shocked than I imagined.</i>

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:30.140
<i>Even though it can be
classified as a weapon,</i>

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:33.640
<i>Miyakoshi did do her best making it.</i>

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:35.100
<i>"Pay me back," huh?</i>

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:39.020
<i>Never mind me. If anyone else
around us is liable to get hurt...</i>

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:41.650
<i>Enough! I'm done
relying on you, Higashida!</i>

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:43.650
<i>I'll feed my chocolate
to the whole world!</i>

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:45.570
If the world ends, it's my fault...

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:49.950
H-Higashida... How can I say this? Um...
Let's all protect the world together!

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:50.950
Adachi...

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.120
Then as someone
with more life experience,

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.660
can I ask you a question?

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:57.450
Even though it couldn't be helped,

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:01.040
what should you do
if you hurt your girlfriend's feelings?

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:03.460
He doesn't know.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:06.550
Don't ask Adachi that.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.630
Don't ask Adachi. No Adachi.

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.220
Muranushi...

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:15.060
When I saw her earlier,
she didn't seem terribly angry.

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:17.140
Why don't you leave her be for a while?

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:17.930
But...

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:21.940
Despite everything you've been through,
you're still kind, Higashida.

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:24.770
And Miyakoshi isn't the nagging type.

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:27.900
Once she's calmed down,
try apologizing again.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.490
Right, Adachi?

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:32.160
Um... I'm sorry!

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:35.330
I don't think it's good
to apologize too much, though.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.040
Adachi, what's up?

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:39.870
You about ready to go on break?

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:40.870
Why?

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:45.500
Why did Muranushi keep pricking me
in the back with a fork?

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.210
Beats me.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:53.050
I don't know, but sounds like she was
in a flirty mood and impatient,

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:56.760
so get back out there and work
in my place for the next hour, Adachi.

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:02.020
Hana, are you okay?
You've been acting strange lately.

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:07.150
E-Ever since you came home from Higashida's
house in the morning with tears in your eyes.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:10.740
Mom... Actually, Higashida and I...

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:16.120
<i>No. If I tell Mom, she'll only worry.</i>

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:18.450
<i>And I should quit asking people
for advice all the time.</i>

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.580
<i>In the first place, I should think
about my apologetic feeling</i>

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.420
<i>and then communicate it to him, right?</i>

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:25.710
Sorry, Mom!

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:28.170
The issue is between me and Higashida.

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:30.340
<i>I'm worried!</i>

00:17:32.760 --> 00:17:37.010
We haven't been working the same shift
for the past few days.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:38.890
I hope Miyakoshi is okay.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:40.180
Higashida!

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:43.560
RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:43.560
I've kept you waiting!
But now I'm gonna pay you back!

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:45.150
<i>Sh-She's gonna kill me!</i>

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:47.980
Miyakoshi, how can I put this?

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:50.400
This is the men's changing room.

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:53.070
This is easier to do
without anyone else around.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:57.740
We'll both feel better the sooner
this is resolved. Take this!

00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:00.120
<i>She's gonna hit me! But should I
just stand here and take it?</i>

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:01.200
I'm sorry.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:04.160
U-Um... Wait.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:07.000
I know it isn't something
that can be fixed with an apology!

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:09.460
BANKBOOK

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:08.290
And here...

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.460
Your bankbook?

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:12.840
I don't know if it's enough to cover
the amount I made you use up to now,

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:14.760
but as compensation, it's all yours!

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:17.390
I didn't know my PIN number,
so I went to the bank.

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:19.470
I filled out some form
I didn't understand,

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.390
and they told me to prove my identity.

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:24.230
The rumors are true about bureaucracy!

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:27.100
Banks that regular people use
are not bureaucracy!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.690
But that's neither here nor there.

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:31.820
Miyakoshi, I need to say something.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.400
<i>She's gonna hit me after all?</i>

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:35.280
R-Responsibility...

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:38.200
I mean, I'm sure you don't want me,

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.240
but I-I-I-I'll take responsibility
and take you.

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:43.950
<i>This conversation is going off the rails!</i>

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:46.870
<i>There's definitely
some misunderstanding here.</i>

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:50.960
<i>Anyway, unless I clear that up
and have her withdraw that proposal...</i>

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:52.300
Um...

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:56.340
<i>Or... this is a rare occasion.</i>

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:59.680
<i>Maybe I'll let it play out a little longer.
Let her feel guilty for a while...</i>

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.760
I'm just sorry, Higashida!

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:02.720
When I think about it,

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:06.140
<i>Miyakoshi regrets and is apologizing
for all of her reckless acts up to now!</i>

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:05.480
I made you eat that chocolate,
forced you to help me study,

00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:09.520
caused you to have a near-death experience,
made you go out with me, and on and on!

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:10.360
OVERWHELMED

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:07.310
<i>Maybe I'll wait until tomorrow</i>

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.520
<i>to clear up the misunderstanding.</i>

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:10.360
To top it off...

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:14.190
you ate chocolate out of my mouth
to save my worthless life!

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.570
Miyakoshi, we really need to talk!

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:20.780
Um... I'll make you happy, so...

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:22.370
Hold on a second, Miyakoshi!

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:22.780
SHAKE SHAKE

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:27.000
You may hate me at first,
but I'll do my best!

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.000
Listen to me!

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:30.830
<i>No good! I can't talk to her
when she's out of her mind!</i>

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:38.260
<i>She came to her senses a little!
Thank you, Adachi!</i>

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.390
I-I-I-I-I'm sorry!

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.470
Now that you've calmed down,
you need to listen to me.

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:45.020
We can just let Adachi go?

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:46.310
Don't look away!

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:51.350
Wha... You didn't get it from my mouth,
but just ate leftover chocolate?

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:55.400
D-Do you know how much I was freaked out
about it? You should've told me!

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.740
You should've listened!

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:59.450
Well, I felt guilty
about squirreling it away,

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:01.570
so I couldn't just come
right out and say it.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:05.790
This is what we get
for being concerned about each other.

00:20:05.790 --> 00:20:07.700
I shouldn't have done that.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:11.670
<i>Still, it was a kick
to see a repentant Miyakoshi.</i>

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:16.800
But to think you felt bad
about not eating all that chocolate...

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:18.800
I'm starving.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.380
Let's get something to eat.

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:21.890
Hurry up and get changed.

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:25.350
<i>And so I'm back to being exploited, huh?</i>

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:26.970
You forgot your bankbook.

00:20:27.270 --> 00:20:28.390
It's on me today.

00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:33.310
Good job!

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:34.690
Good job.

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:36.320
Good job.

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:38.990
Adachi...

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:40.900
What are you moaning about?

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:41.860
Oh...

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:48.120
How can I explain? I'm thinking how lousy
my timing is and how useless I am.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:50.370
Why is that bothering you now,
after all this time?

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:56.000
Leaving that aside, humans mature
when they acknowledge their faults.

00:20:56.290 --> 00:21:00.510
Then I've matured...
so maybe it's a good thing?

00:22:31.510 --> 00:22:33.270
What should we eat?

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:35.140
<i>Miyakoshi's bankbook...</i>

00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:39.770
<i>I should probably give it back to her.
But it's a lot of money.</i>

00:22:39.770 --> 00:22:41.980
<i>To be honest, after getting a look at it,</i>

00:22:41.980 --> 00:22:44.280
<i>I'm not sure whether I should return it.</i>

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:48.530
HANA MIYAKOSHI

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:48.530
<i>After all, her PIN number
is jotted down on the cover.</i>

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:52.790
<i>If I gave it back to her and she lost it,
it'd be a serious problem.</i>

00:22:53.120 --> 00:22:57.000
<i>I mean, it's crazy for me
to hold on to it for her too,</i>

00:22:57.370 --> 00:23:02.750
<i>but I have real doubts about her ability
to safeguard her own bankbook.</i>

00:23:03.510 --> 00:23:06.550
Money can be a very distracting thing.

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:13.390
Your daughter gave this to me,
but I shouldn't have it...

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:16.890
And yet, I'm nervous
about her own ability to keep it safe,

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:19.100
so please hold onto it.

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:23.070
I told Higashida to keep it
as compensation, but he won't listen.

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:36.040
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:30.280
- So, my wish to test myself is coming true.
- Yes.

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:31.700
- So I'll try to study.
- Yes.

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:34.790
Next time,
"The Something Before the Storm."

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:36.040
THE SOMETHING BEFORE THE STORM
